          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fahrschein is built from fahren 'to travel' and Schein 'certificate, slip', both inherited: Schein goes back to Proto-Germanic skīnaną 'to shine' (EtymDB)."
